# Story 23: Layout Mode (Ctrl+L) (45s)
# Hook: Ctrl+L is where you shape your workspace -- resize, equalize, swap, and fullscreen.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-023-layout-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Ctrl+L is where you shape your workspace -- resize, equalize, swap, and fullscreen.

[00:04.0 --> 00:14.0]
Start rysh and split into a few columns so we have something to rearrange.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
Press Ctrl+L to enter layout mode. The footer lists every shaping key.

[00:20.0 --> 00:28.0]
Arrow keys resize the active pane -- Right and Left for width, Up and Down for height.

[00:28.0 --> 00:36.0]
Press equals to balance the widths back out, and m to fullscreen the active pane.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
Press m again to restore, then Escape to leave layout mode. Resize, equalize, swap, fullscreen -- all under Ctrl+L.

